      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For handling aggressive or agitated ED patients, start by maintaining a calm and non-threatening demeanor. Use reflective listening to validate their feelings, such as, \"I can see you are very frustrated right now.\" Keep your language simple, direct, and avoid challenging or arguing with the patient. Remember to actively listen to understand the root cause of their agitation before attempting to resolve the situation.",
